& [FSC3FinalSlicesExplosion] is the processing pass that mints final work slices inside FSC3 runtime graph proof
  + [root_subject] is FSC3 runtime graph proof
  + [chunk_state] is activated_by_FSC2_planning_coordination_pack
  + [boundary_input] is FSC2 planning coordination pack
  + [unresolved_external_dependency_set] is empty_after_gate
  + [slice_strategy] is order slices so imported boundary contracts are mapped before graph contract, checkpoint policy, interrupt/resume behavior, operator trace proof, fixtures, and final pack acceptance
  + [result] is six final slices, one ready now and five gated inside FSC3

  = must: preserve no unresolved dependency outside FSC3
  = must: make each slice contiguous by expected output and verification oracle
  = must: run completed-work review after each completed slice
  = must: mark downstream slices stale when an upstream accepted output changes

## Fold 1: Boundary And Runtime Authority

& [Fold1BoundaryAndRuntimeAuthority] is the boundary check for FSC3 final slices
  + [inside_boundary] is P5 LangGraph procedure runtime and P8c LangGraph runtime, interrupt, and operator-trace fixtures
  + [accepted_boundary_input] is docs/planning/FSC2_Planning_Coordination_Pack.v1.sop
  + [forbidden_external_dependency] is FSC4 surface projection, FSC5 operations safety, live machine control, production dispatch, UI adapter behavior, and unreviewed authority mutation

  = must: import FSC1 and FSC2 packs as accepted boundary inputs
  = must: treat LangGraph checkpoints as execution state and never as source authority
  = must: keep surface projection outside FSC3

## Fold 2: Slice Chain

& [Fold2SliceChain] is the ordered final slice chain
  + [FSC3-S01] is runtime boundary and invariant map
  + [FSC3-S02] is WholeFieldPlannerGraph contract and checkpoint policy
  + [FSC3-S03] is SOP-first interrupt and resume contract
  + [FSC3-S04] is operator trace runtime proof contract
  + [FSC3-S05] is runtime graph fixture plan
  + [FSC3-S06] is FSC3 completion review and activation packet

  = must: keep FSC3-S01 as the only ready slice at first minting
  = must: activate later slices only when their inside-FSC3 inputs are accepted

## Fold 3: Model Routing

& [Fold3ModelRouting] is the route classification for FSC3 slices
  + [FSC3-S01] is requires deeper reasoning
  + [FSC3-S02] is requires deeper reasoning
  + [FSC3-S03] is requires deeper reasoning
  + [FSC3-S04] is requires deeper reasoning
  + [FSC3-S05] is GPT-5.3-Codex-Spark-suitable after FSC3-S01 through FSC3-S04 are accepted
  + [FSC3-S06] is requires deeper reasoning

  = must: state model route on every slice
  = must: keep checkpoint authority, interrupt semantics, and trace proof under deeper reasoning
  = should: route runtime fixture drafting to GPT-5.3-Codex-Spark only after graph and interrupt contracts stabilize

## Fold 4: Readiness And Gates

& [Fold4ReadinessAndGates] is the current FSC3 readiness pass
  + [ready_slice] is FSC3-S01
  + [gated_slice] is FSC3-S02 until FSC3-S01 accepted
  + [gated_slice] is FSC3-S03 until FSC3-S02 accepted
  + [gated_slice] is FSC3-S04 until FSC3-S03 accepted
  + [gated_slice] is FSC3-S05 until FSC3-S04 accepted
  + [gated_slice] is FSC3-S06 until FSC3-S05 accepted

  = must: not start a gated slice until its activation gate is accepted
  = must: run completion review before opening the next slice

& [FSC3FinalSlicesConclusion] is the result of this pass
  + [ready_for] is execution of FSC3-S01 runtime boundary and invariant map
  + [not_ready_for] is LangGraph implementation, surface implementation, operations safety work, or production dispatch
  + [remaining_uncertainty] is graph node shape, checkpoint policy details, interrupt resume semantics, and operator trace proof obligations

  = must: promote the final slice surface only with satisfaction signature and source lineage
